{
  "name": "sdl3",
  "version": "3.4.20",
  "about": "windows, input (keyboard, mouse, gamepads, touch), sound, drawing in 2D, and the GPU",
  "homepage": "https://libsdl.org",
  "license": "zlib",
  "libraries": {
    "windows": "SDL3.dll",
    "macos": "libSDL3.0.dylib",
    "linux": "libSDL3.so.0"
  },
  "downloads": [
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/releases/download/release-3.4.20/SDL3-devel-3.4.20-VC.zip",
      "sha256": "1ec3009655ee37b1f73e52b3b120acc5afd8abaf9532f3303b1bf1dfe91b5969",
      "files": {
        "SDL3-3.4.20/lib/x64/SDL3.dll": "windows64/SDL3.dll",
        "SDL3-3.4.20/lib/x86/SDL3.dll": "windows/SDL3.dll",
        "SDL3-3.4.20/include/SDL3/": "include/SDL3/",
        "SDL3-3.4.20/LICENSE.txt": "LICENSE"
      }
    },
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/releases/download/release-3.4.20/SDL3-3.4.20.dmg",
      "sha256": "36b7e4cefcf7d55d227b3df5e686f8f33ab34193173a976445d1b57c80009e44",
      "files": {
        "SDL3.xcframework/macos-arm64_x86_64/SDL3.framework/Versions/A/SDL3": "macos/libSDL3.0.dylib"
      }
    }
  ],
  "bindings": {
    "alias": "SDL",
    "headers": [
      "include/SDL3/SDL.h",
      "include/SDL3/SDL_main.h",
      "include/SDL3/SDL_vulkan.h"
    ],
    "own": "include/SDL3/",
    "strip": "SDL_",
    "strip_constants": "SDL_",
    "skip": [],
    "clang": [
      "-DSDL_MAIN_HANDLED"
    ],
    "startup": [
      "call SDL.SetMainReady;    # (the program has a start of its own, which SDL is told before anything else of it is called)"
    ],
    "skip_like": [
      "^SDL_PLATFORM_",
      "_h_$",
      "^SDL_COMPILEDVERSION$",
      "^SDL_MAIN_",
      "^SDL_HAS_",
      "^SDL_.*_INTRINSICS$",
      "^SDL_BYTEORDER$",
      "^SDL_FLOATWORDORDER$",
      "^SDL_PRI",
      "^SDL_SIZE_MAX$",
      "^SDL_WINAPI_FAMILY_PHONE$"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "A function is SDL.Name for C's SDL_Name (SDL.Init, SDL.CreateWindow), and a constant the same",
      "(SDL.INIT_VIDEO, SDL.EVENT_QUIT); a struct keeps C's whole name (SDL_Event, SDL_FRect).",
      "An SDL_Event has its type, and the rest is read through a pointer to the kind of event it is:",
      "    ptr<SDL_KeyboardEvent> key: addr event as ptr<SDL_KeyboardEvent>;",
      "SDL's Vulkan functions (SDL.Vulkan_CreateSurface and the rest) take Vulkan's handles as plain",
      "addresses, so a program gives them what vendor.vulkan's functions gave it."
    ],
    "types": {
      "VkInstance": "ptr<u8>",
      "VkPhysicalDevice": "ptr<u8>",
      "VkSurfaceKHR": "u64",
      "VkAllocationCallbacks": "u8"
    }
  }
}
